## Why this is a separate session rather than more of `-01`

`S-2026-08-17-01` performed its LAW-09 close and wrote `L-0000003`. **A session has one
close**, and everything after it belongs to the next session. Recording this work under `-01`
would have made the ledger assert that the close happened after the work it closed, which is
the kind of small untruth this chain exists to make impossible.

## `entry_hash` — DC-3, validated before it was written

DC-3 per `AIEF-AMD-008` §AMD-17: seven covered fields in the declared order, each as one
`<field-name> <SP> <value> <LF>` record, `entry_hash` self-excluded. The implementation was
re-validated against **three** controls first — both worked examples the manifest publishes,
and **`L-0000001` and `L-0000003` recomputed from their own on-disk bytes** to the values
`HEAD` and this entry's `prev_hash` carry. A construction that reproduces both of this
repository's prior entries is not one that was guessed at.

## What this entry records

**The second round refused `ECR-D-014` on a defect the first did not reach.** The ruling was
enforced only on the **preview** path: a mutation skipping the cap check when `canonical` is
true survived all 846 tests, and the canonical build then wrote `core/MANIFEST.lock` and the
`BINDING` pin with a **249-token prefix against a cap of 200**. The cause was structural —
**no test in the repository ever called `run()` with an `Authorization`**, so the only path
that writes canonical bytes had no end-to-end coverage while the preview path had plenty.

Repaired at the source rather than by adding another test at the call site: `run()` now
re-derives the prefix measurement from the octets it actually emitted, immediately before the
only writes that leave the process, and halts on any disagreement. **Six mutations — M8
through M13 — were applied to `build.py` for real and every one is caught.**

**`ECR-D-014` is still not closed**, and for the same reason as at `L-0000003`: LAW-05 bars a
session from certifying its own repair, and no delegation of owner authority reaches a
constitutional separation. It waits on a third cold round and on nothing else.

**A hard limit is now recorded rather than predicted.** `OI-C-10`'s bounded-index runway is
spent: `project/OPEN_ITEMS.md` stands at **597 TF-2 against its 600 cap** after two grammar
reductions in one run, at ~6 tokens per identifier. **The next identifier raised against this
repository breaches `V-09` and halts Stage 6.** No amount of careful writing avoids it.

`sessions/S-2026-08-17-03.md` is the session summary this close produces (`WF-01` Phase 11).
